Program 1: Program to implement a stack using arrays

Algorithm: 
1. Initialization
Step 1: Define a constant MAX as the maximum size of the stack.
Step 2: Create an array stack[MAX].
Step 3: Set top = -1 (indicates an empty stack).
2. PUSH Operation (Insert element)
Algorithm:
If top == MAX - 1 → Stack Overflow (cannot insert).
Else:
Increment top = top + 1.
Set stack[top] = value.
Print "value pushed into stack".
Time Complexity: O(1)
3. POP Operation (Remove element)
Algorithm:
If top == -1 → Stack Underflow (no element to delete).
Else:
Print "stack[top] popped".
Decrement top = top - 1.
 Time Complexity: O(1)
4. DISPLAY Operation (Show elements)
Algorithm:
If top == -1 → Print "Stack is empty".
Else:
Print "Stack elements are: "
For i = top down to 0, print stack[i].
Time Complexity: O(n), where n = number of elements.
5. MAIN MENU (Driver Program)
Repeat until Exit:
Print menu:
1 → Push
2 → Pop
3 → Display
4 → Exit
Input choice.
Perform corresponding operation.

#include <stdio.h>
#define MAX 5   // Maximum size of the stack

int stack[MAX];   // Array for stack elements
int top = -1;     // Top of stack (initially empty)

// Function to push an element into stack
void push(int value) {
    if (top == MAX - 1) {   // Check for overflow
        printf("Stack Overflow! Cannot push %d\n", value);
    } else {
        top++;
        stack[top] = value;
        printf("%d pushed into stack.\n", value);
    }
}

// Function to pop an element from stack
void pop() {
    if (top == -1) {   // Check for underflow
        printf("Stack Underflow! No element to pop.\n");
    } else {
        printf("%d popped from stack.\n", stack[top]);
        top--;
    }
}

// Function to display the stack
void display() {
    if (top == -1) {
        printf("Stack is empty.\n");
    } else {
        printf("Stack elements are: ");
        for (int i = top; i >= 0; i--) {
            printf("%d ", stack[i]);
        }
        printf("\n");
    }
}

// Main program (menu-driven)
int main() {
    int choice, value;
    while (1) {
        printf("\n--- Stack Menu ---\n");
        printf("1. Push\n2. Pop\n3. Display\n4. Exit\n");
        printf("Enter your choice: ");
        scanf("%d", &choice);

        switch (choice) {
            case 1:
                printf("Enter value to push: ");
                scanf("%d", &value);
                push(value);
                break;
            case 2:
                pop();
                break;
            case 3:
                display();
                break;
            case 4:
                return 0;   // Exit program
            default:
                printf("Invalid choice! Please try again.\n");
        }
    }
}

